{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" initial=\"p\">\n  <parallel id=\"p\">\n    <state id=\"left\">\n      <state id=\"l1\">\n        <transition event=\"again\" target=\"l1 l1\"/>\n        <transition event=\"nest\" target=\"left l1\"/>\n        <transition event=\"done\" target=\"done\"/>\n      </state>\n    </state>\n    <state id=\"right\"><state id=\"r1\"/></state>\n  </parallel>\n  <final id=\"done\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml030-nested-and-repeated-targets.scx"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":1,"notes":0,"total":2,"warnings":1},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml030-nested-and-repeated-targets.scx"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":3,"byteOffset":182,"endColumn":48,"endLine":5,"startColumn":45,"startLine":5},"insertedContent":{"text":""}}]}],"description":{"text":"remove the repeated `l1`"},"properties":{"applicability":"machine-applicable"}}],"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml030-nested-and-repeated-targets.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":48,"endLine":5,"startColumn":46,"startLine":5}}}],"message":{"markdown":"transition target `l1` is listed twice\n\n**Note:** a target list names a set of states, so the repeat adds nothing: the state is entered once\n\n**Help:** remove the repeated `l1`\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §3.11 Legal State Configurations and Specifications\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §3.5 <transition>","text":"transition target `l1` is listed twice"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":185,"start":183},"category":"lint"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"first listed here"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml030-nested-and-repeated-targets.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":45,"endLine":5,"startColumn":43,"startLine":5}}}],"ruleId":"SCXML072"},{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml030-nested-and-repeated-targets.scx"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":3,"byteOffset":234,"endColumn":49,"endLine":6,"startColumn":46,"startLine":6},"insertedContent":{"text":""}}]}],"description":{"text":"remove the target `l1`, keeping `left`"},"properties":{"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"}},{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml030-nested-and-repeated-targets.scx"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":5,"byteOffset":230,"endColumn":47,"endLine":6,"startColumn":42,"startLine":6},"insertedContent":{"text":""}}]}],"description":{"text":"remove the target `left`, keeping `l1`"},"properties":{"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"}}],"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml030-nested-and-repeated-targets.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":49,"endLine":6,"startColumn":47,"startLine":6}}}],"message":{"markdown":"transition targets `left` and `l1` are nested: `left` contains `l1`\n\n**Note:** entering `l1` already enters `left`; each target of a multi-target set must lie in a different region of a common <parallel>, so a set that names a state and one of its descendants is rejected by the compiler\n\n**Help:** keep only one of these targets, or place them in different regions of a common `<parallel>` ancestor\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §3.11 Legal State Configurations and Specifications\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §3.5 <transition>","text":"transition targets `left` and `l1` are nested: `left` contains `l1`"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":237,"start":235},"category":"semantic"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"`left` is entered here"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml030-nested-and-repeated-targets.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":46,"endLine":6,"startColumn":42,"startLine":6}}}],"ruleId":"SCXML030"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"the targets of a transition or an `initial` attribute must form a legal state configuration, and the compiler requires each pair to lie in different regions of a common `<parallel>`: targets in different children of a compound `<state>` would require two active children; a target and its own ancestor or descendant name one region twice (a state listed twice is only the `SCXML072` warning)"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: keep only one of the conflicting targets and, when nothing else enters the other state, give it its own transition so it does not become unreachable (`SCXML029`); or move the targets into separate regions of a `<parallel>`. The suggested removal is offered only when it strands no state.\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §3.11 Legal State Configurations and Specifications\n\nRun `scx --explain SCXML030` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#LegalStateConfigurations","id":"SCXML030","name":"SCXML030","properties":{"category":"semantic"},"shortDescription":{"text":"a multi-target set cannot be active at the same time"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"SCXML 1.0 §3.11 defines a legal state specification as \"a set of states such that 1) no state is an ancestor of any other state on the list, and 2) a full legal state configuration results when all ancestors and default initial descendants have been added\": a target list names a set, so a repeated state is legal and is entered once, and the repeat adds nothing"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: remove the repeated target.\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §3.11 Legal State Configurations and Specifications\n\nRun `scx --explain SCXML072` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#LegalStateConfigurations","id":"SCXML072","name":"SCXML072","properties":{"category":"lint"},"shortDescription":{"text":"a target list names the same state twice"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}